{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mathematical pattern mathematical pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md","fileName":"Mathematical Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mathematical Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Sequences and Algebraic Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Law of Formation","Arithmetic Progression","Geometric Progression","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mathematical pattern mathematical pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md","fileName":"Mathematical Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mathematical Pattern","heading":"Mathematical Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A mathematical pattern is a regular relationship among values, positions, or operations that can be expressed with a general rule. Searching for a pattern involves comparing cases, identifying what remains constant, and proposing a [[Law of Formation]].\n\nAlgebra turns the proposed regularity into a formula that can be tested beyond the examples that suggested it. A list increasing by five may lead to an [[Arithmetic Progression]], while repeated doubling may lead to a [[Geometric Progression]]. Observing several matching cases supports a conjecture, but the rule must also explain why the relationship continues.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Law of Formation","Arithmetic Progression","Geometric Progression","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mathematical pattern mathematical pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mathematical Pattern.md","fileName":"Mathematical Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mathematical Pattern","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequences and Algebraic Patterns","Law of Formation","Arithmetic Progression","Geometric Progression","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}